IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg11, Subchapter XVIII:
-- sections 393, 394, 396, 397 and 398 (section 392 is printed [Reserved.]; section 395 is in dg11-s395-trust-in-name.l4).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view; the seat layer dg11-seat.l4 asks these rules as questions.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Quote lines are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N.
--
-- A case the text does not answer is a MAYBE with NOTHING, never FALSE. Money is a NUMBER of United States dollars.

§ `Section 393 - rights, liabilities and duties under prior statutes`

-- src:2084 | All rights, privileges and immunities vested or accrued by and under any laws enacted prior to the adoption or amendment of this chapter, all suits pending, all rights of action conferred, and all duties, restrictions, liabilities and penalties imposed or required by and under laws enacted prior to the adoption or amendment of this chapter, shall not be impaired, diminished or affected by this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 393 (src:2084)
DECLARE `s 393 Kind of thing that an earlier law gave or imposed` IS ONE OF
    `a right, privilege or immunity vested or accrued under an earlier law`
    `a suit pending under an earlier law`
    `a right of action conferred by an earlier law`
    `a duty, restriction, liability or penalty imposed or required by an earlier law`
    `a thing of another kind that s 393 does not name`

-- Gloss: an "earlier law" is a law enacted before the adoption or amendment of this chapter. The text says that the four
-- named kinds "shall not be impaired, diminished or affected by this chapter"; it says nothing about a thing of another
-- kind, or about one that did not arise under an earlier law, so those cases are NOTHING (not covered), not FALSE. (Fork register F-393-1)
-- The other side of the same relation: the holder has the immunity, this chapter (and so the General Assembly acting through it) has the disability.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 393 (src:2084)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 393 Kind of thing that an earlier law gave or imposed`
      `it arises by and under a law enacted before the adoption or amendment of this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` kind `it arises by and under a law enacted before the adoption or amendment of this chapter` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a thing of another kind that s 393 does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `it arises by and under a law enacted before the adoption or amendment of this chapter`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 394 - reserved power of the State; the chapter as part of the charter`

-- src:2088 | This chapter may be amended or repealed, at the pleasure of the General Assembly, but any amendment or repeal shall not take away or impair any remedy under this chapter against any corporation or its officers for any liability which shall have been previously incurred.
-- Gloss: the General Assembly may amend or repeal the chapter (the power is not in doubt and is not a question for a person). What the
-- person is given is the other side: a remedy under this chapter against a corporation or its officers, for a liability already incurred,
-- survives the amendment or repeal. Any other remedy or liability is not addressed, so NOTHING. (Fork register F-394-2)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 394 (src:2088)
GIVEN `the remedy is one under this chapter against a corporation or its officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability was incurred before the amendment or repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394 the remedy survives an amendment or repeal of this chapter` `the remedy is one under this chapter against a corporation or its officers` `the liability was incurred before the amendment or repeal` MEANS
    IF   `the remedy is one under this chapter against a corporation or its officers`
         AND `the liability was incurred before the amendment or repeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2088 | This chapter and all amendments thereof shall be a part of the charter or certificate of incorporation of every corporation except so far as the same are inapplicable and inappropriate to the objects of the corporation.
-- Gloss: the exception needs both limbs ("inapplicable and inappropriate"). Whether a provision is inapplicable and inappropriate to the
-- objects of the corporation is a judgment the text does not assign to anyone; it is taken as two facts the caller states (Fork register F-394-1).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 394 (src:2088)
GIVEN `the provision is inapplicable to the objects of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is inappropriate to the objects of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 394 a provision of this chapter is part of the corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation` `the provision is inapplicable to the objects of the corporation` `the provision is inappropriate to the objects of the corporation` MEANS
    NOT (`the provision is inapplicable to the objects of the corporation` AND `the provision is inappropriate to the objects of the corporation`)

§ `Section 396 - publication of the chapter by the Secretary of State`

-- src:2102 | The Secretary of State may have printed, from time to time as the Secretary of State deems necessary, pamphlet copies of this chapter, …
-- Gloss: the Secretary of State's power to have pamphlet copies printed, as and when the Secretary of State deems necessary (the judgment is the Secretary of State's, so it is a fact the caller states).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 396 (src:2102)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State deems it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 396 the Secretary of State may have pamphlet copies of this chapter printed` `the Secretary of State deems it necessary` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State deems it necessary`

-- src:2102 | and the Secretary of State shall dispose of the copies to persons and corporations desiring the same for a sum not exceeding the cost of printing.
-- Gloss: "the cost of printing" is read as the cost of printing the copy supplied (Fork register F-396-1). The Secretary of State's side of the
-- relation: the person who asks for a copy may be charged no more than that cost; the person's side: a claim not to be charged more.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 396 (src:2102)
GIVEN `the sum charged for a pamphlet copy` IS A NUMBER
      `the cost of printing that copy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` `the sum charged for a pamphlet copy` `the cost of printing that copy` MEANS
    IF   (`the sum charged for a pamphlet copy` AT LEAST 0) AND (`the cost of printing that copy` AT LEAST 0)
    THEN JUST (`the sum charged for a pamphlet copy` AT MOST `the cost of printing that copy`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2102 | The money received from the sale of the copies shall be disposed of as are other fees of the office of the Secretary of State. …
-- Gloss: the money from the sale of the copies is treated as other fees of the office of the Secretary of State (and so, by section 391(a), for the use of the State). The correlative: nobody else is entitled to it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 396 (src:2102)
GIVEN `the money is received from the sale of copies of this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396 the money received from the sale of the copies is disposed of as other fees of the office of the Secretary of State` `the money is received from the sale of copies of this chapter` MEANS
    IF   `the money is received from the sale of copies of this chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2102 | Nothing in this section shall prevent the free distribution of single pamphlet copies of this chapter by the Secretary of State, for the printing of which provision is made from time to time by joint resolution of the General Assembly.
-- Gloss: the text says only that this section does not prevent free distribution of SINGLE copies; it says nothing about free distribution of
-- more than one copy, so that case is NOTHING. (Fork register F-396-2)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 396 (src:2102)
GIVEN `the number of pamphlet copies given out free to one person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396 this section does not prevent the free distribution` `the number of pamphlet copies given out free to one person` MEANS
    IF   `the number of pamphlet copies given out free to one person` EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 397 - penalty for unauthorized publication of the chapter`

-- src:2106 | Whoever prints or publishes this chapter without the authority of the Secretary of State of this State, shall be fined not more than $500 or imprisoned not more than 3 months, or both.
-- Gloss: the offence is printing or publishing this chapter without the authority of the Secretary of State. The penalty is a ceiling, not a tariff:
-- a fine of not more than $500, imprisonment of not more than 3 months, or both.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 397 (src:2106)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 397 the greatest fine for printing or publishing this chapter without authority` MEANS 500

@ref 8 Del. C. § 397 (src:2106)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 397 the greatest term of imprisonment, in months, for printing or publishing this chapter without authority` MEANS 3

@ref 8 Del. C. § 397 (src:2106)
GIVEN `the person printed or published this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had the authority of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 397 the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` `the person printed or published this chapter` `the person had the authority of the Secretary of State` MEANS
        `the person printed or published this chapter`
    AND (NOT `the person had the authority of the Secretary of State`)

-- Whether the penalty is within the section's limits: not covered (NOTHING) for a person who has not committed the offence, because the
-- text gives no penalty for anything else. A fine of exactly $500 and a term of exactly 3 months are inside the limit ("not more than"). (Fork register F-397-1)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 397 (src:2106)
GIVEN `the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397 the penalty is within the limits` `the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` `the fine, in dollars` `the term of imprisonment, in months` MEANS
    IF   `the person has printed or published this chapter without authority`
    THEN JUST (    (`the fine, in dollars` AT LEAST 0)
               AND (`the fine, in dollars` AT MOST `s 397 the greatest fine for printing or publishing this chapter without authority`)
               AND (`the term of imprisonment, in months` AT LEAST 0)
               AND (`the term of imprisonment, in months` AT MOST `s 397 the greatest term of imprisonment, in months, for printing or publishing this chapter without authority`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 398 - short title`

-- src:2110 | This chapter shall be known and may be identified and referred to as the “General Corporation Law of the State of Delaware.”
@ref 8 Del. C. § 398 (src:2110)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 398 the short title of the chapter` MEANS "General Corporation Law of the State of Delaware"

-- "may be identified and referred to as" permits that name; it does not say that no other name is permitted, so a different name is NOTHING. (Fork register F-398-1)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 398 (src:2110)
GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 398 the name may be used to refer to the chapter` name MEANS
    IF   name EQUALS `s 398 the short title of the chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
